cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Se você usar este software ou os seus artefatos, cite-o com os metadados abaixo e cite também o artigo do dataset PublicHearingBR."
title: "bookworm: verifiable evidence units linking structured opinions to public hearing transcripts"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/santana-ai/bookworm"
abstract: >-
  bookworm links each structured opinion of the PublicHearingBR dataset to a
  verifiable span of the public hearing transcript, with exact offsets, the
  rule that chose the span and a separate support confidence from a learned
  verifier. The repository holds the Python library and the reproducible
  experiments on retrieval, confidence and human validation.
keywords:
  - natural language processing
  - portuguese
  - public hearings
  - attribution
  - evidence retrieval
  - natural language inference
authors:
